From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:14:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally give back the later render
 units of idle VMs

With g16_resident_lazy a VM builds one more render unit whenever it has
more render commands outstanding than units, and keeps every unit until
it closes. A compositor that once queued eight frames holds eight units
for good: on a J604 desktop with lazy units, one desktop VM held all
eight and the other three, 715 MiB of pinned memory, where one or two
frames in flight need two units each.

Add the run-time word g16_unit_trim (milliseconds, default 0). At N, a
VM that has had no render command outstanding for N ms first gives back
the units it built after its first render, from the top, down to what
that render built or what the submission needs, before that submission
can name any of them. The trim runs in SUBMIT under the VM's resource
mutex with no job of the VM alive and the build worker held off, so
nothing else reads those units. A unit stays while a flight runs on its
index, a publication is pending there, or the VM's own last render left
the index quarantined, as read under the device lock. The units grow
again on demand as before.

The later units now sit in slots that can be emptied (unit_slot.rs)
instead of SetOnce, with the same reads. The rules are pure functions
in unit_trim.rs. A unit_trim: stats line counts the trims, the units
given back and the trims a unit that could not go yet stopped.

At the default nothing is trimmed and the arena behaves as before.

On this base the later units are sized by RENDER_UNITS, and the stats line
keeps only unit_trim: (the render arena line of the original needs words
this base does not have).

Assisted-by: LLM
